			"type": "text",
			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "m",
				"w": 1747.1302833869706,
				"text": "# Docker Container Execution Flow: CLI to Linux Kernel (Nginx Example)\n\n[User CLI]\n- Command validation: Parses arguments for 'docker run -d -p 443:443 --name nginx nginx:latest'\n- Payloads package: Packages the inputs into an automated JSON payload\n- API transmission: Fires an HTTP POST request over the local engine runtime socket\n\n[dockerd]\n- Phase 1: Request & Validation\n- socket() / accept(): Intercepts the API execution instructions from the client CLI stream\n- open() / write(): Validates image integrity and caches unpacked Nginx filesystem layers\n- Spec generation: Generates the baseline OCI-compliant 'config.json' manifest\n\n[gRPC Socket]\n- Inter-process link: Establishes a local channel at '/run/containerd/containerd.sock'\n- Serialization: Transmits structured Protocol Buffers inside HTTP/2 frames between daemons\n\n[containerd]\n- Phase 2: High-Level Orchestration\n- mount(): Merges read-only Nginx image layers into a single, unified writable 'rootfs' directory\n- Bundle creation: Packs the 'config.json' and 'rootfs' into a standard OCI bundle directory\n\n[containerd-shim]\n- Phase 3: Lifecycle Proxying & Monitoring\n- Process spawning: Launches as a persistent, lightweight daemon dedicated to the Nginx container\n- Stream binding: Keeps standard streams open to capture stdout/stderr logs without daemon lockups\n- Re-parenting: Acts as the sub-reaper parent process to collect the container exit status code\n\n[runc]\n- Phase 4: Boundary Creation & Isolation\n- runc create: Invoked by the shim to initialize the sandbox boundaries using the OCI bundle\n- clone(CLONE_NEWPID | CLONE_NEWNET | CLONE_NEWNS | CLONE_NEWIPC | CLONE_NEWUTS): Creates isolated namespaces\n- mkdir() / write(): Allocates a subsystem path inside '/sys/fs/cgroup/' to cap memory and CPU bounds\n- socket() / ioctl(SIOCSIFADDR): Provisions a virtual network pair ('veth') and configures container IP\n\n[Linux Kernel]\n- Phase 5: Sandbox Lockdown & Nginx Steady State\n- chdir() / pivot_root(): Swaps the host system filesystem tree with the Nginx container 'rootfs' path\n- setsockopt(SO_ATTACH_FILTER): Injects Seccomp filters and AppArmor profiles to secure namespaces\n- capset(): Drops unsafe root permissions while leaving 'CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE' to claim port 443\n- dup2(): Connects container file descriptors 0, 1, and 2 directly to the containerd-shim pipes\n- execve(\"/usr/sbin/nginx\"): Replaces the temporary runc setup process in memory with the Nginx binary\n- runc exit: The runc initialization tool exits completely, leaving Nginx running natively in isolation",
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": false,
				"scale": 1.0045476664506985
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
			"index": "a28VQ",
			"typeName": "shape"
		},
		{
			"x": 17855.451381185667,
