			"type": "text",
			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "m",
				"w": 1393.6152881380403,
				"text": "docker file commands :\n\n# Dockerfile Commands TL;DR Reference\n\n# --- Environment & Setup ---\n- FROM: Sets the base OS/runtime image (e.g., FROM alpine:3.19)\n- ARG: Defines temporary variables valid only during build time\n- ENV: Defines persistent environment variables available during build and runtime\n- WORKDIR: Sets the directory path for all following filesystem actions\n\n# --- Filesystem & Modification ---\n- COPY: Copies local host files/directories into the container filesystem\n- ADD: Copies files, downloads remote URLs, and extracts tar archives automatically\n- RUN: Executes commands inside a sandbox layer to install packages/build code\n\n# --- Configuration & Safety ---\n- EXPOSE: Documents target container network ports (does not publish them)\n- VOLUME: Declares persistent storage mount points (bypassed during build)\n- USER: Drops root privileges; switches to specified user for safety\n\n# --- Execution Entrypoints ---\n- ENTRYPOINT: Sets the unoverrideable main binary executable for the container\n- CMD: Sets default arguments for ENTRYPOINT (easily overridden at runtime)",
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": false,
				"scale": 1.327734643663788
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
